// error: `Buffer[int]` does not conform to `Sendable`, the bound of `T` in `apply`: it is mutable; an immutable copy (`toVector`) is sendable
// error: what is passed for `f` of `Future.map` may use only sendable values from around it, but it uses `b`, a `Buffer[int]`, which is mutable; an immutable copy (`toVector`) is sendable
// error: what is passed for `f` of `Future.onComplete` may use only sendable values from around it, but it captures `seen`, a `var`, which the closure would share with the code that made it; copy it into a `val`, or share it through an `Atomic` or a `Mutex`
// error: `Buffer[int]` does not conform to `Sendable`, the bound of `T` in `Promise`: it is mutable; an immutable copy (`toVector`) is sendable
// error: what is passed for `body` of `Executor.future` may use only sendable values from around it, but it uses `b`, a `Buffer[int]`, which is mutable; an immutable copy (`toVector`) is sendable
// A future's value is sendable; the functions `map` and `onComplete` run on the pool, and a body given
// to an executor, capture only sendable values and no `var`; a promise is of a sendable value.
import avin.threads.{Atomic, Channel, Executor, Future, Promise, spawn}

main()
    val b = Buffer[int]()
    println(Future(Buffer[int]()).await().length)
    println(Future(1).map(x -> x + b.length).await())
    var seen = 0
    Future(1).onComplete(x -> seen = x)
    val p = Promise[Buffer[int]]()
    val ex = Executor.fixed(1)
    println(ex.future(b.length).await())
